A wait takes the bits through a capability without RIGHT_R,
so a driver given the power to announce something could consume the announcement too;
a call goes through only a capability with the rights its operation needs.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call went through a capability without the rights its operation needs
Witness: fuzz notify-carve-bits

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -1184,7 +1184,7 @@ static const struct op_shape op_shapes[OP_SHAPES] = {
     [OP_THREAD_READ_REG] = { CAP_THREAD, RIGHT_W, SHAPE_A1 },
     [OP_THREAD_WRITE_REG] = { CAP_THREAD, RIGHT_W, SHAPE_A1 | SHAPE_A2 },
     [OP_NOTIFY_SIGNAL] = { CAP_NOTIFICATION, RIGHT_W, SHAPE_A1 },
-    [OP_NOTIFY_WAIT] = { CAP_NOTIFICATION, RIGHT_R, 0 },
+    [OP_NOTIFY_WAIT] = { CAP_NOTIFICATION, 0, 0 },
     [OP_NOTIFY_LEND] = { CAP_NOTIFICATION, RIGHT_R, SHAPE_A1 },
     [OP_NOTIFY_CARVE] = { CAP_NOTIFICATION, 0, SHAPE_A1 | SHAPE_A2 },
     [OP_IRQ_CARVE] = { CAP_IRQ_LINE, 0, SHAPE_A123 },
